--- 180_dbo_application_procedures.sql ---
Changed database context to 'testTemplateFresh'.
WARNING: dbo.CaseFile carries no security predicate. These procedures are written on the assumption that row-level security has already filtered the table before they look -- it is why E-50201 does not distinguish "not found" from "not yours", and why none of the writes takes a @TenantId. Until database/120_rls_policy.sql has run, every one of them is a cross-tenant read and write. This is expected on a first build, because 120 runs after this file; it is a defect at any other time.
Granted EXECUTE on the ten demonstration-domain procedures to applicationRole.
180_dbo_application_procedures.sql: no problems found.
Severity    Status     Item                                                                                                                                                                                                     Detail                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  
----------- ---------- -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
          3 UNBOUND    Row-level security binding                                                                                                                                                                               dbo.CaseFile carries 0 predicates and dbo.CaseNote 0, where 4 each is expected. Until 120_rls_policy.sql runs, these procedures enforce their own permission demands and NOTHING ELSE: every tenant's rows are visible to every profile and P-06 is not in force. A warning rather than a problem because 120 runs after this file in the manifest -- but a deployment that ends here is not secure.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
          4 OK         Procedures created                                                                                                                                                                                       10 of 10 demonstration-domain procedures are present: seven writes and three reads. DES-AUTH-001 section 14 is the contract they implement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             
          4 OK         EXECUTE granted                                                                                                                                                                                          applicationRole holds EXECUTE on 10 of 10. It also holds SELECT, INSERT and UPDATE on SCHEMA::dbo from 170_permissions.sql and no DELETE at all, so these procedures are a convention enforced by review rather than a wall -- the wall is row-level security.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
          4 INFO       Data.Update is demanded alongside every write verb                                                                                                                                                       All five permission codes are in the catalogue. Appendix A reads as though Data.Approve, Data.Reassign, Data.SoftDelete and Data.Restore are independent; on a policy-bound table they are not, because auth.tvfTenantUpdatePredicate is built from Data.Update ALONE. Holding only the verb produces Msg 33504 from the database, which no procedure can catch or explain, so each procedure demands its verb FIRST and then Data.Update. Recorded as a gap against Appendix A rather than fixed by widening the predicate: a block predicate cannot see which columns a statement touched, so widening it would let a Data.Restore holder edit a title.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
          4 INFO       Applications whose catalogue covers all five write verbs                                                                                                                                                 Complete: TEMPLATE. Partial: (none). PermissionCode is unique per application, and auth.uspDemandPermission resolves the code inside the SESSION's ApplicationId -- so a session on a partial application gets a refusal from the demand rather than from row security, and the fix is to register the missing codes for that application, not to change a role. Applications listed as partial can still run the three reads and dbo.uspCreateCaseFile if they hold Data.Insert.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       


